 [input]
 
-; Slice S2 input map. ADDITIVE: no setting above this block changes, and
-; `run/main_scene` stays res://tests/SmokeTest.tscn so the harness command still
-; prints PASS 8/8. The game scenes are launched by explicit scene argument.
-;
-; Keys and pad buttons mirror the browser build: `js/main.js:1006-1092` (getInput)
-; and `pollGamepadGameplay` (`js/main.js:789-930`). The one-shot semantics that a
-; key-up carries (space/meta queues the hit on RELEASE, `js/main.js:2573-2580`)
-; are implemented in godot/game/input_map.gd, because ProjectSettings can only
-; express the held state.
-;
-; Menu navigation uses Godot's built-in ui_* actions, which the engine already
-; binds to the arrow keys, the D-pad and the left stick. `ui_accept` and
-; `ui_cancel` are re-declared below as exact SUPERSETS of the engine's defaults
-; because the defaults carry no joypad event for them (measured: a pad-only
-; player could move the focus and had no button to press). No engine event is
-; removed — every keycode event here came out of `InputMap.action_get_events()`.
-
+; BUTTON NUMBERING — read this before touching any button_index below.
+; The browser numbers its pad 0=A 1=B 2=X 3=Y 4=LB 5=RB 6=LT 7=RT 8=back
+; 9=start 10=LS 11=RS 12=up 13=down 14=left 15=right (the Gamepad API's standard
+; mapping, `js/main.js:756-960`). Godot's JoyButton enum agrees only up to Y:
+; 4=back 5=guide 6=start 7=LS 8=RS 9=LB 10=RB 11=up 12=down 13=left 14=right.
+; These bindings carried the BROWSER's numbers for every button past Y, so on a
+; real pad LB paused the match, View switched player, RB and Start did nothing and
+; the D-pad set the wrong tactics. Corrected 2026-09-16; `tests/input/switch_mode_audit.gd`
+; now pins each of these actions to the physical button its own help label names.
